{
  "title": "Sort 0s and 1s",
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "description": "You are given an array `arr` that contains only `0`s and `1`s. Sort it **in place** so that all `0`s come before all `1`s, and return the array.\n\nTry to do it in a single pass with two pointers, without counting.\n\n**Example 1:**\n```\nInput: arr = [1,1,0,1,0,0,1,1,1]\nOutput: [0,0,0,1,1,1,1,1,1]\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n```\nInput: arr = [1,1,1,1,1]\nOutput: [1,1,1,1,1]\n```\n\n**Example 3:**\n```\nInput: arr = [1,0]\nOutput: [0,1]\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n- `0 <= arr.length <= 10^5`\n- `arr[i]` is `0` or `1`",
  "params": [
    {
      "name": "arr",
      "type": "vector<int>&"
    }
  ],
  "compare": "exact",
